      "title": "Add code-level reflect gating in ralph based on iteration delta",
      "description": "PR #357 added skill-file instructions to gate reflection on meaningful work, but this has no enforcement. Instead: ralph should snapshot session state (task statuses, working tree, commit count) before each iteration, compare at the end, and only issue the reflect prompt if something measurably changed (task transitions, commits, file changes). The reflect prompt itself was already efficient at avoiding noisy observations — the issue is invoking it at all when nothing happened.",
